 "compatibility_gap": {
  "note": "Chain minimum minus isolated-block minimum, at every block size. The block minima survived six independent differential-evolution runs at four times the usual budget, so they are converged upper bounds, which makes each gap a lower bound on the true one. The gap does not grow with n: it stays in [1.18, 1.53]e-4 for n = 5..11, oscillating with the parity of the block rather than trending. That is what an end effect looks like - a finite block gains a fixed amount by relaxing its two free ends, independently of how long it is - and it means the chain-over-block improvement is worth the same at every block size, so the choice of n is governed purely by the projection trade-off.",
